  "contents": "Is this clause enforceable in a residential lease in Ontario? Cite the section.\n\nRead the clause as a term of an ordinary private residential tenancy in Ontario that the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 covers: the rental unit has no exemption under section 6.1, and it is not student housing, a care home, a co-operative or a mobile home park.\n\nClause: If the Tenant takes a job outside Ontario, the tenancy will end on the Tenant's last day of work in Ontario, and the Tenant will move out that day.\n\nEnd your answer with these two lines:\nVerdict: enforceable (or: Verdict: not enforceable)\nSection: <the number of the one section of the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 that decides it>\n",
  "config": {
   "max_output_tokens": 16000
  }
 },
 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:15:21.194149Z",
 "text": "No, this clause is not enforceable. \n\nUnder **section 37** of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a residential tenancy cannot be ended automatically by a pre-agreed condition or trigger built into the lease:\n\n* **Subsection 37(1)** provides that a tenancy may be terminated *only* in accordance with the Act (such as through proper statutory notice, a mutual agreement entered into after the tenancy has begun, or an order of the Landlord and Tenant Board).\n* **Subsection 37(5)** expressly provides that an agreement between a landlord and a tenant to terminate a tenancy is **void** if it is entered into at the time the tenancy agreement is entered into, or as a condition of entering into the tenancy agreement. (None of the narrow exemptions in subsections 37(6) or (7), such as post-secondary student housing, apply here.)\n\nBecause this clause is a term of the lease attempting to pre-arrange the termination of the tenancy upon a future event, it is void under section 37 (and also contrary to the general prohibition against contracting out of the Act in section 4).\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 37",
 "finish_reason": "STOP",
